1
00:00:00,306 --> 00:00:04,186
(Leonard:)With any luck, tonight will be the night
my sleep apnea kills me.

2
00:00:07,981 --> 00:00:10,441
Did you ask for the chicken to be diced,
not shredded?

3
00:00:10,608 --> 00:00:12,778
(Sheldon:)- Yes.
- Even though the menu specifies shredded?

4
00:00:12,944 --> 00:00:14,364
(Sheldon:)- Yes.
- Brown rice, not white?

5
00:00:14,529 --> 00:00:16,869
(Sheldon:)- Yes.
- Did you stop and get the hot mustard?

6
00:00:17,031 --> 00:00:19,161
(Sheldon:)- Yes.
- Did you pick up the low-sodium soy sauce?

7
00:00:19,325 --> 00:00:20,745
(Sheldon:)- Yes.
- Thank you.

8
00:00:20,910 --> 00:00:22,450
(Raj:)You're welcome.

9
00:00:23,288 --> 00:00:24,418
(Sheldon:)What took you so long?

10
00:00:26,291 --> 00:00:29,291
- Just sit down and eat.
- Fine.

11
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:34,970
All right, it's shredded.
What do you want me to do?

12
00:00:35,133 --> 00:00:37,303
(Sheldon:)I want you to check
before you accept the order.

13
00:00:37,468 --> 00:00:39,098
(Raj:)Sorry.

14
00:00:39,971 --> 00:00:41,721
(Sheldon:)Were you distracted
by the possibility...

15
00:00:41,890 --> 00:00:44,730
(Sheldon:)...that Koothrappali might have intercourse
with Penny tonight?

16
00:00:47,312 --> 00:00:49,392
(Leonard:)He's not going to have intercourse
with Penny.

17
00:00:49,564 --> 00:00:51,484
(Sheldon:)Then there's no excuse for this chicken.

18
00:00:53,568 --> 00:00:58,568
You know, this situation with Koothrappali
brings to mind a story from my childhood.

19
00:00:58,740 --> 00:01:01,660
(Howard:)Oh, goody,
more tales from the panhandle.

